0..70 Comment "// A machine resumes from its checkpoint and reaches the verdict of an"
71..117 Comment "// uninterrupted run, through `std.reals.Eff`."
118..120 Comment "//"
121..198 Comment "// The program decides `sqrt 2 < 3/2` twice. The first machine runs 16 quanta"
199..277 Comment "// and holds. The second runs one quantum, so it ends `exhausted`. The program"
278..356 Comment "// writes the checkpoint of the second machine: its plan and its steps so far,"
357..430 Comment "// in lowercase hexadecimal. That text is the one form that leaves a run."
431..433 Comment "//"
434..510 Comment "// `restore` validates the text again and mints a third machine. The program"
511..587 Comment "// steps it until it decides, and it holds. Its counters agree with those of"
588..664 Comment "// the first machine: 7 quanta, 2 obligations, and a certificate of 4 steps."
665..738 Comment "// So the certificate replays to the same steps. `gandr run resume.gandr`"
739..797 Comment "// prints `exhausted`, then `holds`, then `the same work`."
798..800 Comment "//"
801..874 Comment "// - see: `corpus/model/reals/comparison.gandr` — the uninterrupted run"
875..954 Comment "// - see: `crates/theory-exact-reals/src/dovetail.rs` — the checkpoint of the"
955..969 Comment "//   scheduler"
971..1003 Comment "// The console\'s host interface."
